> My PC164 needs a new CD drive. IDE appears to be significantly cheaper than 
> SCSI. Can anyone confirm that this system, with latest/last SRM console, 
> will boot and install from ATAPI CD-ROM, both for Tru64 and Linux ?
> ( I believe there were performance issues with this system's IDE, but for 
> the CD drive that doesn't matter very much. Harddisk are all SCSI. )

I have a PC164 running with a IDE disk, CD-ROM, and CD-RW.  The disk
is on IDE channel 0 and boots from SRM 5.5-1.  The CD drives are on IDE
channel 1 and do not show up under SRM.  When I need to install Linux,
I boot off the floppy.  SRM may boot from the CD-ROM if it was on channel
0, but I haven't tried that configuration.  The CD-ROM drive is a
generic 40X ATAPI drive and the CD-RW is an LG CED-8080B.

Bob




