On Sun, Sep 01, 2002 at 04:30:53PM -0500, Ted Goodridge, Jr wrote:
> Where can I get kernel-drm 4.2.0?  That's what is the hold up.  Thanks!

This is a part of kernel and it depends how it was configured and
compiled.  As far as rpm is concerned this particular "provide" comes
from "Provides:" line in specs.  Then you have:

$ rpm -q --whatprovides kernel-drm
kernel-2.4.18-10
kernel-2.4.18-10

and

$ rpm --provides -q kernel
module-info  
kernel = 2.4.18
kernel-drm = 4.1.0
kernel-drm = 4.2.0
kernel = 2.4.18-10

On Alpha you can currently install with '--nodeps' as you are not
likely to really gain anything even if your kernel really does
provide kernel-drm 4.2.0.

  Michal




