On Sun, Sep 01, 2002 at 08:18:02PM -0500, Ted Goodridge, Jr wrote:
> I don't actually want it to install (and yes I read the man page, and
> the howto).

If you want to make a binary package you have to run "%install" macro.
This installs in subdirectories of "%{buildroot}" which is normally
NOT the same as / but some temporary directory.  You can specify
it in a spec file with "BuildRoot" directive but most likely this
is already done.

> I just want to build the binary RPM's.  I did modify the
> specfile.  Does this mean I use the '-ba' switch to just get my packages
> that I can later install?

This indeed will be the way to rebuild binary packages and sources with
your modifications (spec file is a part of sources).  If you did such
changes then you should really adjust "Release" in a spec file (add your
initials?) and make an entry in a "%changelog" section.  Some time from
now when you will start to wonder what you actually modified this will
be an excelent way to check ('rpm -q --changelog ....').

  Michal




