Hello,

Has anybody been able to successfully use RAID-1 on a DP264 machine?

We have posted an issue previously regarding kernel paging errors (Oops
messages), with Red Hat 7.2/7.1 on a alpha DP264 (dual EV6 processors).
We have the problems using stock kernels and as well as custom kernels.
As of right now we are using a custom 2.4.19 kernel.  Thanks to Jay
Estabrook for helping us diagnose the error messages, the "unable to
handle kernel paging request" problems seem to point to the md driver.

Jay also said there are problems while using both channels
simultaneously with the integrated Adaptec controller.  We are currently
using both channels of the Adaptec, one for each drive to get good
performance with RAID-1.  All partitions on on RAID-1 except for the
swap partitions and the /boot partition.  We are also curious if anybody
has a similar setup to this, and if it is working or has known problems.

We've been working on this for over a month, and hopefully close to a
solution.

Thank you for all feedback,

--
Chris




