Okay, I'll comment.  :-)  I do have a 5-port USB hub card in
a UP2000.  It works great.  I have two printers and a scanner
on it at the moment.  With a little care, and a few insmod
commands, I have even hot-plugged in a webcam, but the drivers
don't seem to support the particular camera.

Unfortunately, the original poster said he didn't have any
PCI slots open.  As someone (Maurice?) suggested, maybe an
ethernet adapter from USB would do.  However, watch out for
bandwidth limitations unless you do USB 2.0.

I checked my Jameco catalog, because they usually have a lot
of ISA cards, and they have ISA ethernet but no ISA USB.

Good luck.

Robert Riches
rm.riches@verizon.net

(Oh, and if you buy a USB PCI card or other hardware, the
fine folks at Harddata are great to work with.)




