Hi Folks,

I have installed RH 7.2 from the 4 distribution ISOs (thanks to all for
straightening me out on the downloads) onto my API UP2000+.  I have a
couple of questions I hope members of this list can help me with.

First, a minor annoyance with the install.  It did not by default
install most of the TCP/IP services (telnet, rsh, ftpd), so I had to
go hunting for them in the first 3 CD's.  I did not see any options
for selecting these during the install, with the possible exception
of enabling or disabling firewall (I disabled it since my machine is
already behind a firewall).  I also had to find the sshd server and
manually add that.

Next, some of my users really wanted xemacs, so I tried to install
xemacs-21.1.14-23.7.2.alpha.rpm, but I get the messages:

[root@tb2 RPMS]# rpm -i xemacs-21.1.14-23.7.2.alpha.rpm
error: failed dependencies:
        libcanna.so.1.0   is needed by xemacs-21.1.14-23.7.2
        libRKC.so.1.0   is needed by xemacs-21.1.14-23.7.2
        libwnn6.so.1.0   is needed by xemacs-21.1.14-23.7.2

I could not find RPMs for these libraries.  Can anyone tell me where to
find these?  (I ran into similar problems on my Linux/x86 platforms as
well, and I could not simply copy the files from a system that had it
to the system that did not.)

Another thing, when the system starts to boot, I get a prompt asking me
which boot configuration to use.  The configuration choices are listed
in /boot/etc/aboot.conf.  I would like it to automatically boot from one
configuration all the time, but I'm not sure how to do that.  I thought
there was a file like milo.conf or lilo.conf in /etc, but I see no such
file.

thanks for any assistance,
eyc




