> Another thing, when the system starts to boot, I get a prompt 
> asking me which boot configuration to use.  The configuration
> choices are listed in /boot/etc/aboot.conf.  I would like it 
> to automatically boot from one configuration all the time, 
> but I'm not sure how to do that.  I thought there was a file 
> like milo.conf or lilo.conf in /etc, but I  see no such
> file.

As you pointed out, /boot/etc/aboot.conf is where the options are set. (It's
like lilo.conf) In order to make your system boot automatically, you need to
set boot_os_flags to which ever line in aboot you want to use. 

For example:

set boot_os_flags 0 

would make your system automatically boot using line 0 (console=tty0)

try:

show boot*

and see what boot_os_flags is currently set to. Most likely i (interactive)
or something from a different os ("A" for Tru64 etc)

Cheers,

Collin




