> > From: chu@tes-mail.jpl.nasa.gov (Eugene Chu)
> > Date: Thu,  5 Sep 2002 16:34:02 -0700 (PDT)
> >
> > First, a minor annoyance with the install.  It did not by default
> > install most of the TCP/IP services (telnet, rsh, ftpd), so I had to
> > go hunting for them in the first 3 CD's.

Various network servers (not clients) are not installed by default
on a "workstation" install.  It is easy to add them up if you
are doing a "custom" install.  Even then by default most of servers
will be "off".

> > I did not see any options
> > for selecting these during the install,

If you are picking up one of "canned" configurations then you will
get that.  If you install a number of machines and want a custom
set then investigate how kickstart works.

> Did you install "everything"?

Installing "everything" in nearly all situations is not really a good
thing but one can ask to be allowed to select individual packages
if doing that otherwise is too crude.

> Or, was there such an option on 7.2?

Yes, there is, but if you are using it then most likely you are just
testing the whole distro.

  Michal




