On Fri, Sep 06, 2002 at 09:06:54AM +0200, Linus Gasser wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> just a small question: is ther a tool besides up2date that allows for easy 
> installation of packages and their dependencies?

The "official" one is up2date - of course. :-)  But there are other
options like 'autoupdate', which takes care about dependencies,
http://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/autoupdate/
where you can find links to other project of that sort.
Also Connectiva in their current distro has an rpm aware 'apt',
so I guess that this is out of "experimental" stage, and sources are
freely available.  If you type 'rpm-apt' on Google you should get
quite a few references but I guess that
http://moin.conectiva.com.br/AptRpm
is a good place to start.  Check also
http://apt4rpm.sourceforge.net/home.html

   Michal




