On Fri, Sep 06, 2002 at 07:07:11PM +0300, Iso-H wrote:
> 
> Is there any possibility that PNY's GeForce4
> card: "PNY VERTO GF 4 MX-420 PCI 64 MB" could
> work with 164SX (or with PWS) ??

I think the only way to know is to try it.

If you get a black screen, the answer is NO... ;-}

Historically speaking, it wasn't until nearly the last console
releases (read: BIOS emulator versions) of LX/SX that *any* nVidia
cards would work, and then it was an old TNT2 (ELSA Gloria Synergy
II-32 PCI). PWS/MIATA consoles were not updated as recently...

BTW, that card (TNT2) did NOT work in PWS/MIATA (black screen), but
works quite nicely in an LX164 under RH 7.2, and is very quick in
2D, but will not do 3D (none of the nVidia cards are supported for
3D under XFree86).

Good luck.

 --Jay++

