For what little it may be worth, I have an ES1371-based card
working in a UP2000 with RH7.1 (and 7.0 and 6.1, IIRC).  My
/proc/pci has the following entry:

  Bus  1, device   7, function  0:
    Multimedia audio controller: Ensoniq ES1371 [AudioPCI-97] (rev 8).
      IRQ 47.
      Master Capable.  Latency=32.  Min Gnt=12.Max Lat=128.
      I/O at 0x200008080 [0x2000080bf].

My /etc/modules.conf has the following entries that appear
relevant to the sound card:

alias sound-slot-0 es1371
post-install sound-slot-0 /bin/aumix-minimal -f /etc/.aumixrc -L >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
pre-remove sound-slot-0 /bin/aumix-minimal -f /etc/.aumixrc -S >/dev/null 2>&1 || :

I think I put the first of the entries there, but I don't recall
how the last two got in the file.

Perhaps you have something in the theory that the power surge
did some damage to the motherboard.  :-(

Oh, I'm running stock kernel with modules for the ES1371 (and
just about everything else).  I think it was with RH6.1 or 7.0
that I had to use the ALSA drivers and such, but I think I left
manual installation of ALSA stuff behind with RH7.1.

Good luck.

Robert Riches
