Hi,

What's stopping you from booting directly from SRM???

I've had problems with SB16 sound cards on my old LX where
it would crash the system whenever sound was used. It
'only' happened when I booted from AlphaBIOS/MILO. Switching
to SRM solved the problem. FYI my LX is an old one, Original DEC
and the chipset is one of the first revisions of pyxis. 

Try booting from a floppy from SRM and see if it helps. If not,
the next step I would consider is installing ALSA. 

Peter
