Hi,

I've been getting inquires aprroximately once per month
about status of OpenOffice on AlphaLinux. Daniel left
Compaq a long time ago and I don't have access to my Alpha
yet (due to circumstances beyond my control). As noone has
showed up in dev@porting.openoffice.org mailing list, or
otherwise has stepped up to do the work, my answer remains
the same - I can complete the port as soon as I'll get my Alpha
or get an access to AlphaLinux system with a possibility to install
required binutils/gcc/etc.

For anybody interested:
To get OpenOffice.org going, majority of work would be to make
OpenOffice.org compile and link with the "-taso" option, module
by module, all 80+ of them. He had half of that done with Daniel,
but it was for quite an old revision by now. To make OpenOffice.org
64-bit clean would take a lot of work, in fact, it will be be quite
an accomplishment - note that, umm, _Sun's own_ StarOffice can not
be compiled with -varch=v9a (that is, even for UltraSparc II).

Regards,

Andrei




