>     or price list (etc.) which includes those cards.

We are still seeing Radeon 7000 (AGP and PCI) here in Massachusetts,
in places like CompUSA and BestBuy. Their price epends on the amount
of memory: 32MB is $50-60 US, 64MB is $70-80 US.

Radeon 7500 PCI was never productized by ATI, but we are going to OEM
them (along with AGP versions) for current and future products, at
some point in time, or so I've been led to believe. Those cards are a
very nice step up in performance over the previous PCI Radeons that
I've seen... :-)

And AFAIK, no Radeon beyond the 7xxx series has a PCI version... :-(

But I saw a 9700 PRO ($400 US!) with sticker that said 8X/4X AGP (!)
and an article mentioned it needs a mobo that truly supports the AGP
PRO spec because of it's power requirements.

Sigh - no PCI version of *that* little puppy... ;-}

