Hello,

first this look like something that could use SSE Instruction
on a P4, so with the intel compiler or asm this may get much
faster on the P4.

Then it's all integer, something where the P4 is quite good
at, especially as you don't need to hold a lot of values
in regsters here. And you work on bytes, something that
disables the biggest advantage of the alpha, namely 
the possibility to manipulate 64 bits at a time.

So it's kind of a one-legged race, and since the P4 is 
build from the start one-legged, it excells.

For the alpha, you should enlarge everything to ints.
As far as I have tested, with current compilers, it is
not a goog idea to convert all accesses to pointers,
Just do pN[c] or something like that. The compilers have
more change to do anything with this kind of expression.

To really speed things up, you have to stuff 4 entries
in a long and do this at ones. But this needes some 
serious bit fiddling.

Regards,
Thorsten

