On Thu, Sep 12, 2002 at 10:19:02AM -0400, Shoshana Rosenthal wrote:
> 
> I would like to restore tar tapes from a remote tape drive.
> Both machines run ssh and xinetd.

   ssh -l <tape_access> <remote> "dd if=<tape_device" | tar -x

or something similar.  You may use netcat to transport data over
a network.

With gnu tar at least you can simply do something like

tar --rsh-command=/usr/bin/ssh -f <tape_access>@<remote>:<tape_device> -x

but this expects 'rmt' in a "proper" place on <remote> and possibly that
you can autologin via ssh without supplying a password ("known_hosts").
It is all in documentation.

What this has to do with Linux on Alpha?

  Michal




