"Donsbach, Jeff" <Jeff.Donsbach@hp.com> writes:

> Some applications make assumptions about page size and hard code
> things instead of using programatic methods of determining it. Could
> lead to strange behavior if the page size is different from what the
> app is expecting.

Only the page size doesn't change; it stays at 8k. The difference is
that when 8 pages are allocated continuously, the kernel sets a hint
for the TLB that the mapping is for 8 continuous pages, so 7 entries
in the TLB are saved. Except for timing differences (and bugs ;), this
should be impossible to detect for an application.

-- 
	Falk




