APC Cable Wiring 

that works, and I got this:
http://www.sibbald.com/apcupsd/3.8manual/cables.html

which should answer just about all the cabling questions as it shows the 
pinout for both the simple and the smart cables.

Smart signaling is used on the higher-end UPS's (such as the smart series 
and higer) to relay real-time data such as voltage and temperature. The 
computer can also relay back to the UPS to run self tests, shut down, 
power back up, etc. It's the one that's closest to a real serial 
connection with the pinout messed up.

Simple signaling is used on lower end UPS's (such as the Back UPS's) and 
mainly just to tell the software very basic things such as low battery, on 
battery and a signal from the computer back to the UPS to shut down.

I have a Smart UPS 1400 here and it just 'works' in linux / windows on 
both intel and AXP. I use the actual APC daemon in x86 linux, and run 
upsd on the AXP one as APC doesn't want to come out with an AXP version of 
its software =/.

Kurt

