The only real difference is the 'smart signaling' cable and the 'simple 
signalling' cable. (of course the wiring for the simple cable is much more 
complicated than the smart cable... go figure).


APC came up with the different spec for the wiring because of the fact 
that many of their higher end UPS's have a serial console on them as well, 
that runs through the same port on the UPS as the signalling to the 
computer. So.... naturally they messed with the pinout to make this 
feasable and so you'd have to use their cables. IIRC the 'smart UPS' 
models have the console enabled when you install the remote management / 
web interface / remote alert card installed in the expansion slot. (I 
forget the real name of it, and I have yet to play with mine as I'm only 
running a few servers off my 1400).

Kurt


