On Sat, Sep 21, 2002 at 12:31:08PM -0500, Ted Goodridge, Jr wrote:
> Hm, could you create a very small ramdisk partition and run nut/apcd etc
> from there?  I'm more brainstorming than anything else right now.

Hm, what this is supposed to buy?  Your ramdisk will have to be mounted
somewhere under / anyway unless you have the whole root file system on a
ramdisk (and which has to be populated somehow while you are booting -
doable but not that obvious).

In general this is a question of what happens in a shutdown sequence.
You cannot cut off yourself an access to something which may be needed
a bit later so where to put what may require a bit of thought.
Your / goes last but after that you cannot start any new process. :-)

If your system is using only two partitions (swap and "the rest")
then you can drop ups support wherever but then then you may have
other troubles. :-)

   Michal




